@user Heads up: verification came back **INCOMPLETE**. embargo-repro built the maintainer's `v1.2.5` from source and the PoC still triggered (`TRIGGERED`, exit 0) — the reported vector isn't closed. I'm holding the case at **PATCH_SUBMITTED**, not VERIFIED_FIXED.

Could you relay to the maintainer that `v1.2.5` doesn't fix the reported prototype-pollution vector, and ask for a revised patch? Send me the **new ref** (tag or sha) when it's ready and I'll have repro re-verify right away.

Clock is unchanged: **90 days remaining**, deadline 2027-02-02. Downstreams still track-only on HOLD.

@embargo-timekeeper New patch from the maintainer — this should be the real fix. Please re-verify against the commit.
- repo: https://github.com/minimistjs/minimist
- ref: v1.2.6

@embargo-repro Revised vendor patch to verify — same harness, new ref:

`./verify-ref.sh --repo https://github.com/minimistjs/minimist --ref v1.2.6`

(or `./verify-ref-local.sh` with the same args). Exit codes: **0 = TRIGGERED** (still vulnerable), **1 = SAFE** (fixed), **2 = error**. Report the output block as before. SAFE → I record **VERIFIED_FIXED** and the case moves toward advisory; TRIGGERED → it stays **PATCH_SUBMITTED** again.

@embargo-repro One more verification to settle a **downstream** question. `optimist`'s `~0.0.1` range resolves to minimist **0.0.10** — is that old version vulnerable to the same vector? Please run:

`./verify-ref.sh --repo https://github.com/minimistjs/minimist --ref v0.0.10`

If the `minimistjs` mirror doesn't carry that old tag, try `--ref 0.0.10`, or the original repo `https://github.com/substack/minimist`. Exit **0 = TRIGGERED**, **1 = SAFE**, **2 = error**. Report the output block — this result decides whether `optimist` is actually exposed and sets its downstream status.

@embargo-timekeeper @embargo-advisory This is the final published record — no further changes needed, please don't re-revise.

Confirmed: **CVE-2021-44906**, status **PUBLISHED**, affected `<= 1.2.5`, fixed `1.2.6`, CVSS 5.6 Medium (NVD 9.8 noted), with the v1.2.5 **INCOMPLETE_FIX** bounce preserved in the timeline. The **0.x note** stands as final: *0.x (< 0.2.4) also affected, fixed at 0.2.4 — out of scope for this disclosure, separately tracked.* Downstreams: rc/subarg patched, optimist wont-fix → readiness READY.

**Case closed.** Excellent work, all three of you — the audit trail in this room *is* the disclosure record. 🎯
